"segments": [
{
"start": 0.03,
"end": 5.0,
"text": " on this side, Macaulay Cuck is on this side, his sister's in there, we're all just jamming the bed."
},
{
"start": 5.02,
"end": 8.55,
"text": "Then we wake up like dawn and go in the hot air balloon."
},
{
"start": 9.42,
"end": 10.86,
"text": " You know, we have the footage."
},
{
"start": 11.12,
"end": 12.36,
"text": "I have all that footage."
},
{
"start": 12.4,
"end": 13.74,
"text": "But is that right, Michael?"
},
{
"start": 14.0,
"end": 14.8,
"text": "It's very right."
},
{
"start": 15.58,
"end": 16.46,
"text": "It's very loving."
},
{
"start": 16.48,
"end": 17.9,
"text": "That's what the world needs now."
},
{
"start": 18.42,
"end": 21.22,
"text": "More love, more heart."
},
{
"start": 21.24,
"end": 25.52,
"text": "The world needs a man who's 44, sleeping in a bed with children."
},
{
"start": 25.62,
"end": 27.06,
"text": "No, you're making it all wrong."
},
{
"start": 27.44,
"end": 28.14,
"text": "Well, tell me."
},
{
"start": 28.16,
"end": 28.52,
"text": "Help me."
},
{
"start": 30.18,
"end": 31.65,
"text": " What's wrong with sharing a love?"
},
{
"start": 32.57,
"end": 37.89,
"text": "You don't sleep with your kids or some other kid who needs love, who didn't have a good childhood?"
},
{
"start": 37.91,
"end": 38.45,
"text": "No, no, I don't."
},
{
"start": 38.91,
"end": 40.49,
"text": "I would never dream of sleeping."
},
{
"start": 40.69,
"end": 43.71,
"text": "I would never dream... Because you've never been where I've been, mentally."
},
{
"start": 43.97,
"end": 45.69,
"text": "What do you think people would say if I..."
},
{
"start": 47.15,
"end": 53.29,
"text": " and said, well, I've invited some of my daughter's friends round or my son's friends round and they're going to sleep in the bed with me tonight."
},
{
"start": 53.41,
"end": 54.09,
"text": "That's fine."
},
{
"start": 54.11,
"end": 55.31,
"text": "What do you think their parents would say?"
},
{
"start": 55.91,
"end": 58.07,
"text": "If they're wacky, they would say, you can't."
},
{
"start": 58.21,
"end": 62.84,
"text": "But if you're a close family, like your family, you know them well."
},
{
"start": 62.86,
"end": 69.96,
"text": "But Michael, I wouldn't like my children to sleep in anybody else's bed."
},
{
"start": 70.59,
"end": 79.46,
"text": " Well, I wouldn't mind if I knew the person well, and I... Like, if I'm very close to Barry Gibb, Paris and Prince can stay with him any time."
},
{
"start": 79.76,
"end": 81.8,
"text": "My children sleep with other people all the time."
},
{
"start": 82.42,
"end": 83.16,
"text": "And you're happy with that?"
},
{
"start": 83.42,
"end": 84.06,
"text": "Fine with it."
},
{
"start": 84.58,
"end": 85.16,
"text": "They're honest."
},
{
"start": 85.2,
"end": 86.06,
"text": "They're sweet people."
},
{
"start": 86.3,
"end": 87.4,
"text": "They're not Jack the Ripper."
},
{
"start": 87.92,
"end": 94.07,
"text": "I suppose the problem for many people is what happened in 1993, or what didn't happen."
},
{
"start": 94.49,
"end": 95.35,
"text": "What didn't happen."
},
{
"start": 97.43,
"end": 98.59,
"text": "Just cast your mind back."
},
{
"start": 99.73,
"end": 103.25,
"text": " What was that like when you first heard the allegations that were being made against you?"
},
{
"start": 104.11,
"end": 107.22,
"text": "It was shocking and I'm not allowed to talk about this by way of law."
},
{
"start": 108.26,
"end": 110.18,
"text": "But how did you feel about what was being said?"
},
{
"start": 110.22,
"end": 111.86,
"text": "I'm not asking you to talk about what was said."
},
{
"start": 112.7,
"end": 113.96,
"text": "I was shocked because..."
},
{
"start": 116.77,
"end": 119.25,
"text": " God knows in my heart how much I adore children."
},
{
"start": 119.39,
"end": 125.25,
"text": "But isn't that precisely the problem, that when you actually invite children into your bed, you never know what's gonna happen?"
},
{
"start": 125.29,
"end": 128.43,
"text": "But when you say bed, you're thinking sexual."
},
{
"start": 128.61,
"end": 129.67,
"text": "They make that sexual."
},
{
"start": 129.71,
"end": 130.79,
"text": "It's not sexual."
},
{
"start": 131.35,
"end": 132.17,
"text": "We're going to sleep."
},
{
"start": 132.51,
"end": 133.37,
"text": "I tuck them in."
},
{
"start": 133.39,
"end": 137.63,
"text": "I put a little, like, music on and a little story telling."
},
{
"start": 137.66,
"end": 138.31,
"text": "I read a book."
},
{
"start": 138.86,
"end": 139.4,
"text": "It's very sweet."
},
{
"start": 139.42,
"end": 141.52,
"text": "Put the fireplace on, give them hot milk."
},
{
"start": 142.08,
"end": 143.3,
"text": " You know, we have little cookies."
},
{
"start": 143.4,
"end": 145.34,
"text": "It's very charming, very sweet."
},
{
"start": 145.36,
"end": 145.74,
"text": "Sure."
},
{
"start": 145.92,
"end": 147.32,
"text": "It's what the whole world should do."
},
{
"start": 147.9,
"end": 155.08,
"text": "The reason that's been given for why you didn't go to jail was because you reached a financial settlement with the family."
},
{
"start": 155.5,
"end": 156.14,
"text": "Yeah, yeah."
},
{
"start": 156.68,
"end": 163.52,
"text": "I don't want to do a long, drawn-out thing on TV like OJ and all that stupid stuff, and it wouldn't look right."
},
{
"start": 163.74,
"end": 165.3,
"text": "I just said, look, get this over with."
},
{
"start": 165.32,
"end": 166.48,
"text": "I want to go on with my life."
},
{
"start": 166.96,
"end": 167.78,
"text": "It's just ridiculous."
},
{
"start": 167.8,
"end": 168.46,
"text": "I've had enough."
},
{
"start": 169.88,
"end": 170.02,
"text": "Go."
},
{
"start": 171.58,
"end": 178.44,
"text": " I questioned him much further, but the confidentiality agreement he signed means we cannot show that part of the interview."
},
{
"start": 178.98,
"end": 181.2,
"text": "My questions had upset him deeply."
},
{
"start": 183.72,
"end": 188.0,
"text": "People don't even eat with their fathers anymore, or their mothers."
},
{
"start": 189.91,
"end": 191.65,
"text": " The family bond has been broken."
},
{
"start": 192.55,
"end": 196.74,
"text": "It's an outcry for attention, why kids are going to school with guns."
},
{
"start": 197.78,
"end": 200.86,
"text": "They want love, they want to be touched, they want to be helped."
},
{
"start": 200.88,
"end": 210.54,
"text": "They're busy off on their day job and they leave them at home on the computer and they're just doing all kind of crazy stuff and that's destroying our world."
},
{
"start": 211.68,
"end": 213.12,
"text": "We need to bond again."
},
{
"start": 213.14,
"end": 216.16,
"text": "That's very important, Martin."
},
{
"start": 217.04,
"end": 218.34,
"text": "Why does it mean so much to you?"
},
{
"start": 221.61,
"end": 229.15,
"text": " I'm just very sensitive to their pain, and I'm very sensitive to the family, the human condition on that subject."
},
{
"start": 230.25,
"end": 235.09,
"text": "It means a lot to me, and I want to help do whatever I can to help that."
},
{
"start": 238.03,
"end": 248.52,
"text": "Like I said before, and I've said it a million times, I'm not afraid to say it, if there were no children on this earth, if somebody announced, all kids are dead, I would jump off the balcony immediately."
},
{
"start": 248.96,
"end": 249.42,
"text": "I'm done."
},
{
"start": 250.52,
"end": 250.86,
"text": "I'm done."
},
{
"start": 255.72,
"end": 262.58,
"text": " And so I left Michael Jackson."
}
]
}